59,3,,status,George,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,George,,Option A seems too much like the policing I mentioned; tracking every single distance will likely lead to the same friction we saw when checking figures. I'm leaning toward a simpler approach.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Toshio,,Option A is exactly the kind of administrative nightmare I'm worried about. Tracking every kilometer and calculating costs per booking would only increase the time we spend on paperwork and untangling debts.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"Option B provides the most stability. If I know the car is mine on a specific day, I can ensure it's ready for my needs without worrying about how the previous person left it.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"Option B is the most straightforward for the budget. A fixed monthly share removes the need to track every single liter of fuel, which prevents the resentment caused by uneven contributions.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Minato,,"Option B sounds very peaceful because we wouldn't have to argue about the money every time. But if we have fixed days, will the people with those weekly clashing trips still be able to use the car?","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,George,,"@Minato, that is a valid concern. However, if we use Option B, we can simply swap days with each other. A friendly agreement to trade is much healthier than a rigid ledger of debts.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"Swapping days is a flexible solution, but it still requires coordination. However, compared to the constant calculations of Option A, Option B is far more efficient. It eliminates the weekly hour of administrative labor.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@George, I agree that swapping is possible, but the real benefit of Option B is the predictability. Knowing exactly when the car is available removes the anxiety of wondering if it will actually be there and ready for me.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Victoria, I agree. Predictability is key. From a financial perspective, Option B is the only one that truly solves the subsidization issue. It treats the share as a share, making the costs transparent and equal for everyone.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Minato,,"I see. If we can just swap days when we need to, then Option B sounds very kind. It makes the money part simple too, so we don't have to guess who paid for what.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,George,,"I believe Option B is the most sustainable choice. It avoids the ""accountant"" atmosphere of Option A and the potential for resentment in Option C, allowing us to maintain our friendship while sharing the car.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"Option B is the most logical choice. It minimizes the time spent on coordination and eliminates the tedious process of squaring receipts, which is the most draining part of this arrangement.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Victoria,,"I agree. Option B is the only one that guarantees a baseline of reliability. It allows us to take personal responsibility for the car's state on our assigned days, ensuring it's actually usable.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"I agree. Option B is the most balanced choice. It provides the financial clarity I'm looking for without the constant friction of tracking every single trip, which is the most sustainable way to avoid quiet subsidization.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Minato,,"I think Option B is the best. It feels the most fair and calm for everyone, and it means we can stop guessing about the money. I'll vote for B!","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,George,,I agree with everyone. Option B protects our relationships by removing the need for constant policing and calculations. It is the most mature way to handle this. I vote for B.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Toshio,,"Option B is the only choice that effectively removes the administrative burden. It replaces tedious calculations with a simple, predictable structure. I vote for B.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Victoria,,Option B is the only way to ensure the car is actually ready when I need it. It replaces uncertainty with reliability. I vote for B.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Misaki,,"Option B is the most rational solution. It ensures a fair, equal split of the costs and removes the ambiguity that leads to resentment. I vote for B.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Minato,,I'm so happy we all agree! It makes me feel relieved that we found a way to be fair and stay friends. I vote for B too!,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
